WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.400
-It is great to see you, buddy.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.801
We met a few -- a few years ago.
-Yes.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.834
-And you also --
you know The Roots, as well.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.200
-I do know The Roots.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.501
Tariq, Amir.
What's up, everybody?

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:10.634
-Yeah.

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.467
-Black Thought,
what's happening? Stro.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:13.767
Yeah, they worked on
my first special.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.934
-That's wild. It's almost
like a whole family here.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.000
-It is a family situation.
You got a beard now.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.234
You're copying me.
It's beautiful.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.067
-I am, yeah, no.
-Don't ever get an edge up

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.367
like Tariq, though.
Like Black Thought.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.634
Don't ever do it.
-Don't do that.

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:25.934
-I don't think
it's the look for you.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.000
-No.
-You should have the patchy --

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.601
It's nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.868
-Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.601
Thank you very much.
-And it adds all the layers.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.767
Yeah. You, uh --
You said that you're a fan,

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.767
obviously, of "The Tonight Show"
but also NBC

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.734
and "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.033
I didn't know
you're a big "SNL" fan.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.567
-I'm a huge "SNL" fan.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.234
Like, when I first
started stand-up,

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.400
I would imitate
Chris Farley in class.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.801
Like, that's where I would wear
a little jacket

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.801
and just -- yeh yeh --
walk around like this.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.434
[ Laughter ]
And I met him.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:54.801
I met him
when I was 13 years old.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.801
They had Planet Hollywood's
grand opening.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.167
You remember those?
-Yeah.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.434
-Didn't last long, but at least
I got to meet Chris.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.834
-That was a big deal.
-That was a big deal.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.267
-Stallone and Schwarzenegger.
-Yeah, Stallone walks up,

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.434
and he's like, "Hey, yo, kid."

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.534
I'm like,
"Get outta here Rambo."

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.300
[ Laughter ]
I'm just --

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.067
I really was.
I could care less.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.234
Schwarzenegger's walkin' up,
like, "Hey."

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.601
I was like,
"Get outta here. You too."

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:15.868
-You just want to see...

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.634
-I just wanted to see the chubby
guy I relate to so much.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.100
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.133
And I see him, and I shake his
hands, and I wouldn't let go.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.868
[ Laughter ]
And I was like, "I love you!"

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.100
And he was like,
"I love you, too!"

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.267
And I was like,
"I love you more!"

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:29.701
And he was like,
"Let go of my hand!"

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.968
I was like, "Grb-rb-rb-rb-rb!"

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.667
And it was, like,
the best moment of my life.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.567
-The best thing ever.
Look at you now, bud.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.801
I gotta say,
I want to talk about your show,

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.667
But also you're in the big new
hit movie, "Black Adam,"

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.033
that's coming out,
with The Rock.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.968
Yeah, it's a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:51.701
-Yeah.
-How is Dwayne doing?

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.534
We love Dwayne Johnson.
-Do we love Dwayne Johnson?

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.367
-Yeah. Yeah, we love him.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.300
-We do?
-We love Dwayne Johnson.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.400
-We do. We love him!
He's just so perfect.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.701
-I know.
-Just annoyingly perfect.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.701
-He's the best.
-Promoting everything

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.901
all the time, and we want it
'cause he's so good at it.

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.767
-Yeah.
-Always just -- he's big --

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.133
I saw him.
We were doing content days.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.267
And he walks up and,
"Mo, how you doing?"

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.467
I was like, "I'm doing good.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.868
You're always out here
promoting all this stuff.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:20.567
Like, how good is it?"
And he takes out a ZOA,

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.000
and he hands it to me,
pop it open,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.734
he's like, "Cheers."
"Cheers."

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:27.234
And I drank it.
I was like, "Man, this is

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:30.133
really delicious,
and I don't feel any jitters

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:33.000
or anything like that.
This is really outstanding."

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.767
And I look up, and there's
a three-camera shoot.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:38.300
I'm like, "I just do a free
commercial for The Rock?"

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.400
[ Laughter ]
-He's that good!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.434
-He's a mad genius!
-He's that good!

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:45.534
-Did I see a penny?
-No.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.834
-But I did get like
nine cases of ZOA, though,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.334
so I appreciate that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.801
-And you're in the movie, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.701
-Can we talk about "Mo," though?
This is a big deal.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:56.901
Streaming right now on Netflix.
Inspired by your own life.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:59.167
How close is it
to your real life?

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:05.000
-It's really grounded in my
experience coming to America

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.400
as a refugee, asylee,
from a Palestinian background.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.133
It's very grounded in that case.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.501
I will say I'm not addicted
to lean -- very important.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.334
'Cause it's in the show.
It's a big --

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.133
It's one of those layers
in the show.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.767
It's really important.
I want that on blast, Quest.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.100
You know what I'm saying?
-You want everybody to know

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.400
that that's not you.
You're not addicted, no.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.601
-Yeah, Quest, he saw the show,

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.267
he's like, "I didn't know
Mo was addicted to lean."

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.033
I'm not!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.534
-I called you.
-The show is about a refugee,

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:32.200
you know,
trying to assimilate in America,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.834
trying to feel seen
and feel equal

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.267
to the person next to them.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:39.767
It's a deeply personal story.
It's never been done before.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.467
-I read this today.

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.834
This is the first-ever
American-made show?

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:48.267
-It's the first-ever show
created by, starring

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.934
a Palestinian and showing

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.367
a Palestinian family
on television.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.100
So it's a really big deal.
-Yeah, good for you, bud.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you, man.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.901
-Congratulations.
That's awesome.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.100
And I will say it's --

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.567
On Rotten Tomatoes right now,
you're 100%.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.767
Certified Fresh!

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:07.501
Certified Fresh!
-Yeah.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.267
-Congratulations.
It's a great show.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:10.734
-And another thing --
it was the first-ever

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:13.501
narrative sitcom
to be filmed in Houston.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.701
When we're such a big exporter
of music --

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.901
Beyoncé, what's up?
Hit me up.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.234
-What do you mean hit you up?
-And Lizzo --

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.601
-I just want to say hi.
Jay-Z.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:22.801
It's like,
we're both from Houston.

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.634
We should know each other.
-Okay, okay, yeah.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:29.334
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:30.801
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:33.567
Here's Mo Amer in "Mo."
Take a look at this.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.334
-What you doing
over at Lakewood?

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.400
-Oh, we're, uh,
in a gospel, uh, choir.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.634
-International.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.868
Actually, showcasing
the diversity of Houston.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.200
-Yeah, diversity initiative.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.567
I know that's
one of those things.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.634
Yeah, I got that e-mail.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.133
-Well, if you're
a couple gospel singers,

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:50.067
why don't you, uh,
sing a few hymns for me?

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:51.934
-Oh, yeah.
Of course.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.400
We can do that.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.234
-We can do that.
-[ Clears throat ]

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:56.767
Uh...

00:04:56.767 --> 00:05:02.634
♪ Oh, precious is the flow... ♪
-♪ ...is the flow ♪

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:08.200
♪ That may seem white as snow ♪
-Yeah.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:14.767
-♪ No other fount I know ♪

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:20.968
♪ Nothing but the blood
of Jesus ♪

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.334
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.367
-The flow?
[ Laughs ]

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:27.534
-We tried.
-Here's what --

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:30.033
Here's what's great.
'Cause it's funny,

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.267
but that is actually
based on something

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.801
that happened in your real life.
-Maybe. Uh...

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.667
[ Laughter ]
No, it did.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:39.000
The story came from -- I was
driving this two-lane highway.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.968
It was pitch black,
and I was going to a gig.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:45.601
And I missed the exit, so I make
this very illegal U-turn.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:46.901
And I realize
I'm running out of space.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.000
There's, like,
a bayou right there.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.667
So I put my car in reverse.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.534
And this other car is screaming,
coming at me, I was like,

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.300
"Oh, no!" and it just missed me,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.167
and the car crashes
into a ditch.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.033
And I pull forward, I was like,
"Oh, my God.

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:59.667
I'm such an idiot.
I hope this person's okay,"

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:02.133
and they drive out of the ditch,
and they park behind me.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:05.234
I was relieved, and then he
turned on his police lights.

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.868
And I may or may not
have pot in the car, you know?

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:11.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.033 --> 00:06:12.434
I'm a comedian.
I'm sorry.

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:14.534
And the cop runs up to me,

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:16.667
and he's just irate.
Understandable.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.067
He's like, "What the hell's
the matter with you?!

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:19.901
You're an idiot!"
I'm like, "Yes, sir!

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:21.667
Yes, sir,
I'm such a huge idiot!"

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:22.968
He's like, "You're a moron!"

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.968
I was like, "Couldn't agree
with you any more."

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.767
[ Laughter ]
"Such a moron!"

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:28.901
And then he knew
that he was speeding

00:06:28.901 --> 00:06:31.968
and he could've killed me.
He was like, "Oh, man,

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:35.133
I don't know how -- I don't know
how I didn't kill you."

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:37.934
I was like, "I know how."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.834
It's 'cause of our
Lord and savior Jesus Christ.

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.167
That's how."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.100
[ Speaking Arabic ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.634
-And there you go.
You turn it into a show.

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.634
-And I let it go.
-Mo Amer, everybody.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:49.467
His series, "Mo,"
is streaming now on Netflix.

